 ## Background
-Hybrid representations emerged to address the limitations of pure Neural Radiance Fields (NeRF), which are compute-intensive for real-time rendering, and pure explicit methods, which lack the flexibility of continuous representations. The concept of storing features in a structured format (voxel grids, hash tables) and decoding them via lightweight networks was introduced to balance memory efficiency and rendering speed [S1]. Notable implementations include MERF, which introduces a baking procedure to transition from an optimized hash-grid representation to a real-time renderable format [S1]. Not given in the sources for other historical details or sibling comparisons.
